    "body": "Note: there are ~2 types of non-fully-active documents. The first is a document in bfcache. The second is one without a browsing context, e.g. created by `new Document()`. This issue is about the latter, because you can't run JS in the former.\r\n\r\nI wonder if it'd be web-compatible to throw for `showModal()` in non-fully active documents. It's pretty nonsensical anyway.\r\n\r\nBut, the simplest path is to probably just no-op the close watcher step.",
